## When modular clocks agree

The [Chinese remainder theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_remainder_theorem) explains compatibility. Two classes $a\pmod m$ and $b\pmod n$ have a common member exactly when $a\equiv b\pmod{\gcd(m,n)}$.

