<details><summary>Click to reveal the compatibility argument</summary>
Write $m=du$ and $n=dv$ for $d=\gcd(m,n)$. Agreement modulo $d$ makes $b-a=dt$. Because $u$ and $v$ are coprime, $uy\equiv t\pmod v$ has a solution. Then $x=a+my$ satisfies both original congruences.
</details>

## Search for new certificates

Discovery can be treated as [set cover](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Set_cover_problem): each valid modular rule covers a subset of residues, and the goal is to cover the entire period.

